<article class="max-w-3xl space-y-12">
  <%= render "charts/header", page: "donut", lead: "A pie with the total in its middle: stock by warehouse, the month's spending. Use it when the total matters as much as how it splits." %>

  <section class="space-y-10">
    <h2 id="examples" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Examples</h2>
    <%= render "charts/example", id: "total", title: "With its total", example: "donut/basic",
               text: "type: :donut. The middle shows the sum of the slices, written the same way as the values." %>
    <%= render "charts/example", id: "money", title: "Money", example: "donut/money",
               text: "With format: :currency, the slices, the legend and the total are all written as money." %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 id="notes" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Notes</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>Everything on the <%= link_to "pie chart", chart_doc_path("pie"), class: "text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline dark:text-fuchsia-300" %> page applies: one series, up to five slices, nothing below zero.</li>
      <li>The total's size follows the hole, so it stays inside it on a small chart.</li>
      <li>For a single figure on its own, such as today's sales, show the number rather than a donut of one slice.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <%= render "docs/pager", previous_page: [ "Pie chart", chart_doc_path("pie") ], next_page: [ "Components", components_path ] %>
</article>
